      <div class="content">
        <section class="panel agenda-panel" id="agenda" aria-labelledby="agenda-title">
          <div class="panel-inner">
            <div>
              <p class="section-kicker">Agenda</p>
              <h2 class="section-title" id="agenda-title">Power, institutions, technologies.</h2>
              <p class="section-copy">
                My work connects historical sociology and sociotechnical analysis to examine how
                governance is built, contested, and redesigned. Across archives, public services,
                classification systems, digital platforms, and AI, I study how authority is organized
                and how vulnerability is produced.
              </p>
              <p class="section-copy secondary-copy">
                I bring extensive international experience, strong academic networks, and a
                trajectory marked by a Marie Skłodowska-Curie Actions Postdoctoral Fellowship,
                doctoral support linked to the University of Chicago, and publications with
                Cambridge University Press, Oxford University Press, MIT Press, American
                Behavioral Scientist, and other leading venues.
              </p>
              <div class="prestige-strip" aria-label="Academic affiliations and venues">
                <span>MSCA Fellow</span>
                <span>University of Chicago</span>
                <span>Cambridge University Press</span>
                <span>Oxford University Press</span>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="agenda-line" aria-hidden="true">
              <img class="agenda-image" src="/agenda/agenda-scr.png" alt="" loading="lazy" />
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="panel dark research-panel" id="research" aria-labelledby="research-title">
          <div>
            <p class="section-kicker">Research</p>
            <h2 class="section-title" id="research-title">Three clusters, one question.</h2>
            <p class="section-copy">
              How do institutions, classifications, and technologies organize power, produce
              vulnerability, and reshape governance?
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="cluster-grid">
            <a class="cluster-card" href="/research/#governance" aria-label="View governance, corruption, and institutional power research cluster">
              <span class="cluster-number">01</span>
              <svg class="cluster-motif" viewBox="0 0 260 180" aria-hidden="true">
                <path d="M28 145 H230" />
